<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicolas Durand de Villegaignon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1510">1510</a>–<a href="/years/1571">1571</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicolas Durand de Villegaignon was a French naval officer and Knight of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a> who in 1555, backed by Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspard-de-coligny">Gaspard de Coligny</a>, founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> Antarctique in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanabara-bay">Guanabara Bay</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. He built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-coligny">Fort Coligny</a> on an island, but religious quarrels with Calvinist settlers divided the colony and he returned to France in 1559. The Portuguese destroyed it and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicolas-durand-de-villegaignon.jpg" alt="Nicolas Durand de Villegaignon" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicolas Lagneau · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicolas_Lagneau_-_Nicolas_Durand_de_Villegagnon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
